+# The Daily Grind
+
+A responsive account security page with real WebAuthn passkey registration, passwordless sign-in, management, and reauthentication.
+
+## Run
+
+Requires Node.js 22 or newer.
+
+```sh
+pnpm install
+pnpm start
+```
+
+Open `http://localhost:11222`. Create an account using **Set up a passkey**, then use your authenticator's fingerprint, face, PIN, or security key prompt. Sign out through My account and use **Sign in with a passkey** to return. Add a second passkey before removing your first.
+
+## Configuration
+
+- `PORT`: server port, defaults to `11222`.
+- `APP_ORIGIN`: exact public origin, for example `https://coffee.example.com`. Set this when using a reverse proxy. Passkeys require HTTPS except on localhost and are tied to the configured hostname.
+- `DATA_DIR`: persistent storage directory, defaults to `.data`. Back it up and restrict its filesystem access. It contains account data and public credential records; private keys and biometrics never leave the authenticator.
+
+Account records persist to disk. HTTP-only, SameSite session cookies expire after 24 hours. Sessions and single-use, five-minute challenges live in memory; restarting the server signs users out. Deploy as a single server instance, or move these stores to a shared database and session service before horizontal scaling. Email is an account identifier; this app does not verify email ownership or provide email-based recovery. Register backup passkeys to retain access after losing a device.
+
+Management changes require an identity verification within the last five minutes. The server verifies origin, RP ID, challenge, signature, user verification, credential ownership, and signature counters using SimpleWebAuthn. Removing the last passkey is blocked to prevent account lockout.
+
+## Automated verification
+
+```sh
+pnpm test
+```
+
+Tests use a cryptographic P-256 authenticator fixture, not mocked verification. Coverage includes registration, login, signature rejection, replay rejection, ownership checks, stale reauthentication, renaming, removal, last-passkey protection, logout, and backup credential login. No manual browser verification is required.
